From: Xios Project <xios@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Do not query missing ssh tool paths when the agent is disabled

Meson returns a not-found program object when ssh_agent=false, but calling
.path() on that object is still an error. Keep the configured paths empty for
the iOS client-library-only build.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -52,8 +52,10 @@ if p11_system_config_modules == ''
   error('Couldn\'t find location for pkcs11 module config')
 endif
 libsecret_dep = dependency('libsecret-1', version: '>= 0.20', required: get_option('ssh_agent'))
-ssh_add_path = find_program('ssh-add', required: get_option('ssh_agent')).path()
-ssh_agent_path = find_program('ssh-agent', required: get_option('ssh_agent')).path()
+ssh_add = find_program('ssh-add', required: get_option('ssh_agent'))
+ssh_add_path = ssh_add.found() ? ssh_add.path() : ''
+ssh_agent = find_program('ssh-agent', required: get_option('ssh_agent'))
+ssh_agent_path = ssh_agent.found() ? ssh_agent.path() : ''
 
 with_systemd = false
